A||||9||DR650SE||Short throw-1--2 shift is really tough||||9||
Z||000000||DR650SE||11-05-2001||11:59 PM||||I have a short throw in one of my 86 SE  4-speeds.  It makes the shift from 1-2 really hard to hit.  This is slowing my 0-60 times down ALOT.  Isn't it supposed to improve the time?  Is something wrong?  Thanks.<BR><P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||9
Z||000001||My7Fieros||11-06-2001||01:17 AM||||I shortened the shifter in my 86 GT....really short. In fact, I pulled out the old "mile high" shifter, and actually installed a roughly 6 inch metal down and welded it into the location of the orginal handle. It only sites maybe 1 1/2 inches from bottom of (aftermarket) knob to ashtray level....same prob. In fact, I usually have to SLAM it into first, otherwise itll pop out of gear! eek.<BR>BTW whats the deal w/ your quarter mile times? Is this car a daily driver or some kind of a race car?||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero_nightmare||11-06-2001||05:26 AM||||i shortened the shifter on my 85 GT 2 inches. at first it was the same way but after i put some white lithium grease everywhere that moves on the shifter and shifter cables (both ends) it got pretty easy. <P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <BR> <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fiero_nightmare (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_24||11-06-2001||07:48 AM||||You shortened the shifter, but you decreased the amount of leverage.  I had a short shifter in my 86SC, and the day I sold it I took it out.  It was so much easier to shift with the old shifter back in place.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||4
