Z||000008||revin||11-06-2001||02:08 PM||||rodney adds a longer "plate" where the cable attaches to the shifter. I think that is what ya'll need to do when you shorten the shifter.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pontiaddict||11-07-2001||12:53 AM||||Moving the shifter should be nearly effortless at the stock height. If you think that it would be really hard to move your shifter with a shortened handle, chances are you need to lube your shift cables or even replace them.<P>DR650SE, it sounds like you have a cable adjustment or linkage problem. If you have a repair manual, follow the instructions for adjusting the cables.<BR>||||reg||1
